          "lines": [
            0,
            61,
            122,
            188,
            251,
            312,
            372,
            437,
            497,
            556,
            621
          ],
          "text": "Note that I am introducing a new “compound” type, because in this case there is no location associated with the top-level object. In cschem, it is possible that a container exists without virtual elements and vice versa. The above syntax allows that. Normally, containers live in the “container:” namespace, but that is not enforced. Likewise, contained elements normally live in the “virtual:” namespace, but that is also not enforced. For instance, it would be entirely reasonable to combine an LED and a photo-NPN into a container. I don’t know whether “U1.L”, “U1.Q” are valid part names, but if not, I can make that possible in the future.",
          "uuid": "941cedf1"
        }
      ]
    },
