          "lines": [
            0,
            63,
            127,
            192,
            255,
            315,
            376,
            440,
            504,
            564
          ],
          "text": "are valid in names, but “.” is used to separate bus names from contained lines. I use “–” which needs to be replaced by “-”. I use “.” in part names which can be replaced with “,”. Can I also replace “/” with “,”? A cschem name “A1:3/−” and “A1.3:–” must not map to the same kicad name. Perhaps “A1,3_-” and “A1_3,–” is appropriate? That is, there is a comma between part and pin and underscores within parts and within pins. So “A1.2:3/–” becomes “A1_2,3_-”. I think I like a hyphen better: “A1_2-3_-”, even though that means that a simple “A1:-” becomes “A1--”. I’m ok with that.",
          "uuid": "6cd16c98"
        }
      ]
    },
